## Create or extend the Angular workspace

Scaffold apply renders the deterministic equivalent of Angular CLI output. It
does not execute Angular CLI.

For this repository, this scoped workflow overrides the emitted
`angular-new-app` skill's generic npm/npx single-application bootstrap
defaults. Use the Bun empty-workspace sequence below so no root `src/`
application is created.

For a manual recreation, start from the repository root with an empty Angular
workspace so Angular never creates `{frontend.root}/src`:

```bash
bunx @angular/cli@22 new {{angular.defaultApplication}}-workspace --directory {frontend.root} --no-create-application --new-project-root {{relativePath frontend.root frontend.appsRoot}} --package-manager bun --skip-install --interactive=false
```

Then run application generation from `{frontend.root}` with the explicit
destination and resolved options:

```bash
{{#each angular.applicationNames as this}}
bunx @angular/cli@22 generate application {{this}} --project-root={{relativePath frontend.root frontend.appsRoot/this}} --skip-tests --standalone --strict --zoneless --style={angular.styleMode} --ssr={angular.ssr} --interactive=false
{{/each}}
```

Routing is resolved as `{angular.routingMode}`: add `--routing` when enabled
or `--no-routing` when disabled. Do not accept an interactive default. Add
libraries with the same discipline under `{frontend.libsRoot}`; never use
Angular CLI's root application layout.
